(149865, 7733, 3942, '<td valign="top">Oops,<br/><br/>please excuse my mistake in ''shadow''.  As I wrote alredy in my user details I use the dpc to learn more about photography and to improve my english. So I welcome your constructive criticism on both! But now the whole world is able to see my asininity on the main page of dpc this week.  Sometimes a 3rd place can be embarrassing too :-)<br/><br/>Thanks to all the users, who took the time to make a comment and special thanks to po_the_great. Your german is better than my english ;-)<br/><br/>Please have a look on the photo details above for some more informations about this shot. If there are more questions, please feel free to ask me!<br/>@ mac: No no, not deliberately...<br/>@ bmac: No, its not a collage. Only a calendar and some pulled sheets...<br/>@ TrexX: Is it not ''instead'' instead of '' in stead'' :-) :-) :-)?<br/>@ KAOS, PTLParsons: The shadow is the number 12. Thats why I titled ''Shadow of a lucky day''. Is the number of the shadow really so hard to realise? <br/><br/>Thanks again, your really made my day!<br/>Matthes</td>', 'Oops,please excuse my mistake in ''shadow''.  As I wrote alredy in my user details I use the dpc to learn more about photography and to improve my english. So I welcome your constructive criticism on both! But now the whole world is able to see my asininity on the main page of dpc this week.  Sometimes a 3rd place can be embarrassing too :-)Thanks to all the users, who took the time to make a comment and special thanks to po_the_great. Your german is better than my english ;-)Please have a look on the photo details above for some more informations about this shot. If there are more questions, please feel free to ask me!@ mac: No no, not deliberately...@ bmac: No, its not a collage. Only a calendar and some pulled sheets...@ TrexX: Is it not ''instead'' instead of '' in stead'' :-) :-) :-)?@ KAOS, PTLParsons: The shadow is the number 12. Thats why I titled ''Shadow of a lucky day''. Is the number of the shadow really so hard to realise? Thanks again, your really made my day!Matthes', '2002-11-11 14:01:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(149866, 7733, 2221, '<td valign="top">Congratulations brother! Now we''re on par again *grrr* ;-) Great photo!</td>', 'Congratulations brother! Now we''re on par again *grrr* ;-) Great photo!', '2002-11-11 16:32:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(149867, 7733, 2283, '<td valign="top">WOW! Really Really Really Nice man, I cant say I could do this myself, this truly impresses me.  I dont know why people dont see the 12, I spotted it pretty quickly, the 13th is deffinately brought to the forefront by the darkness of the number though, my question though is how did you capture the page lifting and produce the effect that the calender book is above the sheets? I would love to know how you did this in detail.. Impressive!</td>', 'WOW! Really Really Really Nice man, I cant say I could do this myself, this truly impresses me.  I dont know why people dont see the 12, I spotted it pretty quickly, the 13th is deffinately brought to the forefront by the darkness of the number though, my question though is how did you capture the page lifting and produce the effect that the calender book is above the sheets? I would love to know how you did this in detail.. Impressive!', '2002-11-13 03:06:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(149868, 7733, 3942, '<td valign="top">No problem, the setup was relatively simple. Unfortunately I haven''t made an extra shot of the whole setup. But I think you''ll get it, when you turn the photo 180 degrees in your mind. The sheets are lying scattered on the floor and the calendar is standing upside down on them. So the reason for the little page lifting was after my helping hand only the gravity. More information about the shadow of the ''12'' and the lighting you''ll find in the photo details. O.K.?</td>', 'No problem, the setup was relatively simple. Unfortunately I haven''t made an extra shot of the whole setup. But I think you''ll get it, when you turn the photo 180 degrees in your mind. The sheets are lying scattered on the floor and the calendar is standing upside down on them. So the reason for the little page lifting was after my helping hand only the gravity. More information about the shadow of the ''12'' and the lighting you''ll find in the photo details. O.K.?', '2002-11-13 16:21:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(149869, 7733, 5121, '<td valign="top">Nice tone. It has a "Stan Lee" graphics look to it. Impressed.</td>', 'Nice tone. It has a "Stan Lee" graphics look to it. Impressed.', '2002-11-15 16:58:00.000000', NULL, 0),
