(150515, 7782, 4186, '<td valign="top">sometimes i just don''t get why things get voted the way they do. this one was my favourite shot this week. i gave it a ten. and it came in last.<br/><br/>i think it''s composed interestingly, has nice colors, good lines, and yes -- fulfills the challenge. has anyone ever seen the kinds of pictures normally taken of ufos? alot of them happen to look exactly like this, only not as artistic.<br/><br/>i am a firm believer in two things: the abstract, and the random shot. and i happen to love this photo.<br/></td>', 'sometimes i just don''t get why things get voted the way they do. this one was my favourite shot this week. i gave it a ten. and it came in last.i think it''s composed interestingly, has nice colors, good lines, and yes -- fulfills the challenge. has anyone ever seen the kinds of pictures normally taken of ufos? alot of them happen to look exactly like this, only not as artistic.i am a firm believer in two things: the abstract, and the random shot. and i happen to love this photo.', '2002-11-11 14:30:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(150516, 7782, 2221, '<td valign="top">I agree with Arachnophilia here. I didn''t score it as high as a ten but an 8. I think it suffers from bad JPEG compression but I liked the blur and the colours. The abstract and "snapshot" look fits perfectly to the idea of the photo. Don''t let you down Emil, IMHO your photo was way better than many others in this challenge. Keep on photographing!</td>', 'I agree with Arachnophilia here. I didn''t score it as high as a ten but an 8. I think it suffers from bad JPEG compression but I liked the blur and the colours. The abstract and "snapshot" look fits perfectly to the idea of the photo. Don''t let you down Emil, IMHO your photo was way better than many others in this challenge. Keep on photographing!', '2002-11-11 19:34:00.000000', NULL, 0),
