(151380, 7851, 2221, '<td valign="top">Very nice photo. Cool lighting! Composition is also good. That makes me even more sad that the photo suffers from bad JPEG compression. Your photo is only only 32 kB big, so I think you saved the file with high JPEG compression and low quality. Remember that you can use up to 150 kB here on DPC. -stephan</td>', 'Very nice photo. Cool lighting! Composition is also good. That makes me even more sad that the photo suffers from bad JPEG compression. Your photo is only only 32 kB big, so I think you saved the file with high JPEG compression and low quality. Remember that you can use up to 150 kB here on DPC. -stephan', '2002-11-10 15:34:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(151381, 7851, 4493, '<td valign="top">For those of you who gave this a low score due to jpg artifacts and poor focus, here is a link to the version I ment to upload. //www.pbase.com/image/6821219<br/><br/>Live and learn,<br/>-crabappl3</td>', 'For those of you who gave this a low score due to jpg artifacts and poor focus, here is a link to the version I ment to upload. //www.pbase.com/image/6821219Live and learn,-crabappl3', '2002-11-11 07:41:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(151382, 7851, 2221, '<td valign="top">Thanks, crabappl3. Really looks better that way. I didn''t give you a bad score for the JPEG artifacts (just 1 point off).</td>', 'Thanks, crabappl3. Really looks better that way. I didn''t give you a bad score for the JPEG artifacts (just 1 point off).', '2002-11-11 19:49:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(151383, 7853, 3540, '<td valign="top">This is a well taken photo.  I''m not sure I like the composition.  If the focus was just on the eye why use the foreground "cover" to hide the rest of the cat.  It looks dark enough where if the background were dark, we wouldn''t be able to see him anyway.  The negative space in the shot would be accenting the eye much more than the distracting table or whatever it is.  IMO - Inspzil</td>', 'This is a well taken photo.  I''m not sure I like the composition.  If the focus was just on the eye why use the foreground "cover" to hide the rest of the cat.  It looks dark enough where if the background were dark, we wouldn''t be able to see him anyway.  The negative space in the shot would be accenting the eye much more than the distracting table or whatever it is.  IMO - Inspzil', '2002-11-04 04:56:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(151384, 7853, 4829, '<td valign="top">Very nice!</td>', 'Very nice!', '2002-11-04 09:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
