(151635, 7867, 1041, '<td valign="top">you are raising a deep philosophical question here ... you say you didn''t submit a photo because they steal souls, but then the admin note says this is indeed a digital photo.  did you steal your lens cap''s soul?  does a lens cap have one?  how can you live with yourself?   :)<br/>-- gr8photos</td>', 'you are raising a deep philosophical question here ... you say you didn''t submit a photo because they steal souls, but then the admin note says this is indeed a digital photo.  did you steal your lens cap''s soul?  does a lens cap have one?  how can you live with yourself?   :)-- gr8photos', '2002-11-08 12:21:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(151636, 7867, 2716, '<td valign="top">Ok.  I''ll give a 3 for having a title that fits the challenge.  Jacko.</td>', 'Ok.  I''ll give a 3 for having a title that fits the challenge.  Jacko.', '2002-11-08 17:14:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(151637, 7867, 5106, '<td valign="top">The urban myth which bothers me the most....lol. Nice submission.</td>', 'The urban myth which bothers me the most....lol. Nice submission.', '2002-11-08 22:39:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(151638, 7867, 811, '<td valign="top">Ummm, the focus is a little off, and don''t you think the crop is too tight.  Maybe if you converted it to black and white, rotated it 90 degrees to the left, then flipped and mirrored it, it would be more interesting.  Oh yea, and you should have adjusted the curves a little more.  Otherwise, great shot. karmat</td>', 'Ummm, the focus is a little off, and don''t you think the crop is too tight.  Maybe if you converted it to black and white, rotated it 90 degrees to the left, then flipped and mirrored it, it would be more interesting.  Oh yea, and you should have adjusted the curves a little more.  Otherwise, great shot. karmat', '2002-11-08 23:41:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(151639, 7867, 3540, '<td valign="top">Well thought out.  Creative.  I had this same idea but since I have no camera to keep the lens cap on when I shot it, I couldn''t produce this photo.  Hopefully I''ll get it back though.  The focus is perfect.  Can''t argue with the DOF.   I think you''re better off shooting this at a higher aperture though with a lower ISO, for mood purposes.  The dark filter is probably not necessary in this one but adds a nice touch.  Great use of negative space without an actual subject to focus on.  Definitely the best black picture this week.  I bet you could use this as a Macro of your lenscap.  This pic will probably have a cult following.  I''ll join the "Club" :) - Inspzil</td>', 'Well thought out.  Creative.  I had this same idea but since I have no camera to keep the lens cap on when I shot it, I couldn''t produce this photo.  Hopefully I''ll get it back though.  The focus is perfect.  Can''t argue with the DOF.   I think you''re better off shooting this at a higher aperture though with a lower ISO, for mood purposes.  The dark filter is probably not necessary in this one but adds a nice touch.  Great use of negative space without an actual subject to focus on.  Definitely the best black picture this week.  I bet you could use this as a Macro of your lenscap.  This pic will probably have a cult following.  I''ll join the "Club" :) - Inspzil', '2002-11-09 05:38:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(151640, 7867, 3031, '<td valign="top">Even digital camera''s? ;-))</td>', 'Even digital camera''s? ;-))', '2002-11-09 06:59:00.000000', NULL, 1),
